This product includes software developed as part of the PrismaLens project
(https://prismalens.io).

The npm package bundles third-party software in two places:

1. The web dashboard. Its third-party code and licences are listed in
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt, next to this file.

2. The agent adapters, under node_modules/@prismalens/agent-adapters/. They
   let an installed Claude Code or Codex answer the Agent Client Protocol:
   - @agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp, @agentclientprotocol/codex-acp and
     @agentclientprotocol/sdk (Apache-2.0);
   - @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk, under Anthropic's own terms rather than
     an open-source licence. Its LICENSE.md reads: "© Anthropic PBC. All
     rights reserved. Use is subject to the Legal Agreements outlined here:
     https://code.claude.com/docs/en/legal-and-compliance";
   - @openai/codex, the Codex CLI package codex-acp depends on (Apache-2.0,
     as its package.json declares), without its platform binaries;
   - their dependencies (MIT and BSD-3-Clause).
   Each keeps its own licence file in its package directory, except
   @openai/codex, which ships none.

Everything else the package needs, npm installs next to it from the registry,
each with its own licence file.
